{
  "slug": "blinking-beacons",
  "title": "Blinking Beacons",
  "statement": "There are `n` beacons. Beacon `i` flashes at every moment `t ≥ 0` with `t mod p[i] = r[i]`, that is, at the moments `r[i]`, `r[i] + p[i]`, `r[i] + 2·p[i]`, and so on.\n\nFind the earliest moment `t ≥ 0` at which all `n` beacons flash together.",
  "inputFormat": "Line 1: one integer `n`.\nThe next `n` lines: line `i` holds two integers `p[i]` and `r[i]`, separated by a single space.",
  "outputFormat": "Print one integer: the earliest moment at which all beacons flash together. If that never happens, print `-1`.",
  "constraints": "1 ≤ n ≤ 1000\n1 ≤ p[i] ≤ 1000000000000000000 (10^18)\n0 ≤ r[i] < p[i]\nThe least common multiple of all p[i] is at most 10^18.",
  "topic": "math",
  "difficulty": "hard",
  "timeLimitMs": 2000,
  "samples": [
    {
      "input": "2\n3 2\n5 3\n",
      "explanation": "Beacon 1 flashes at 2, 5, 8, 11, ... and beacon 2 flashes at 3, 8, 13, ... The first common moment is 8. Answer: 8."
    },
    {
      "input": "2\n4 1\n6 4\n",
      "explanation": "Beacon 1 flashes only at odd moments (1, 5, 9, ...) and beacon 2 only at even moments (4, 10, 16, ...), so they never flash together. Answer: -1."
    },
    {
      "input": "3\n4 3\n6 1\n10 7\n",
      "explanation": "At moment 7: 7 mod 4 = 3, 7 mod 6 = 1 and 7 mod 10 = 7, so all three flash. Checking 0 to 6 shows no earlier common moment. Answer: 7."
    }
  ],
